"position":{"commit_sha":"d0f18a02c667f57231221c61d16f66c2ca0d3cc4","position":"1795061918564850045-92085caf-224e-4d88-8046-8d9838d42242"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a50d4a599b2d046263432341895afb07e3131131b62fcf7b45f063a3a52652e7","event_uuid":"c0182566-0c3e-4fe7-a6a3-38e03c5c2e2b","position":{"commit_sha":"28c0b5126ab62f94297ff08e23b597867ca71452","position":"1795062037921716224-c0182566-0c3e-4fe7-a6a3-38e03c5c2e2b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"3fb24987930e60c870b26bd0539e85e513a71ec687887db20965049d711c1d38","event_uuid":"ea04f988-b553-489f-83bf-ecaa019e241b","position":{"commit_sha":"2fcf4008c1246057e468b0dcd86f075a54e0ef3d","position":"1795062467081260506-ea04f988-b553-489f-83bf-ecaa019e241b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"4008d24d29802b01dbfc513db346d11e3ff5f6df68ae92d1e7f8e4e472246be3","event_uuid":"72f3c015-9c49-4db6-ab3a-c453ca98d3b1","position":{"commit_sha":"d210defa35f21496d6cdaf250125f80b0e9c10ea","position":"1795062475164686296-72f3c015-9c49-4db6-ab3a-c453ca98d3b1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Not a 0.16.0 release blocker, so I removed the release-0.16.0 tag. rebar has never had `--version` (v0.15.1 lacks it too). `docs/releasing.md` \u00a75 doesn't list it in the smoke test, and nothing delivered in 0.16.0 touches it. Adding it means adding a new CLI flag or subcommand, so it's a feature decision for the operator, not a bug fix. The options the release-candidate checker proposed: (1) a top-level `--version` printing the version and commit; (2) a `rebar version` subcommand with `-o json`; (3) close as wontfix. This ticket stays open until the operator chooses.","timestamp":1794616832015890077},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Bug-cluster session 3d705fec, 2026-11-18: not worked. Every fix option adds a new top-level CLI flag or subcommand, which the bug-fix rule (no new config key, env var or flag in a fix) excludes without an operator decision, and no option has been chosen on this ticket yet. Still awaiting an operator choice among: (1) add top-level `--version` printing `rebar <version> (<commit>)` from importlib.metadata and rebar._build_info.COMMIT, plus probes in scripts/probe_rebar.py and the release wheel_test job; (2) add a `rebar version` subcommand with the same output and `-o json`; (3) record the absence as intended and close wontfix, dropping `rebar --version` from release check lists.","timestamp":1795033775550306313},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Operator decision (2026-11-18): option (1)\n\nAdd a top-level `rebar --version` that prints `rebar <version> (<commit>)` from importlib.metadata and rebar._build_info.COMMIT, with probes in scripts/probe_rebar.py and the release wheel_test job. The operator explicitly approves this new CLI flag as an exception to the bug-fix no-new-flags rule. It is a standard CLI convention, and the release checklists already reference it. Options (2), a `rebar version` subcommand, and (3), wontfix, are rejected.","timestamp":1795051090799808198},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Session 05f74084: implemented option (1) at commit 4dced0093d6 (worktree kestrel-version-05f74084, on origin/main 6f5f854be4c). Root cause: `_help_route.pre_scan` answered only help/overview/unknown forms, so `--version` fell to `_emit_unknown`. Fix: a `--version` branch there printing `rebar <version> (<commit>)`. RED: 3 new tests in tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py failed before the fix; GREEN: 16 passed. make lint exit 0 (mechanism gate exits 0 with no marker needed: a CLI argv token is not one of its 7 kinds). probe_rebar.py: 144 passed, 0 failed. Wheel built with `uv build --wheel` installed in a fresh venv: `rebar --version` -> `rebar 0.16.0 (6f5f854be4c)`, exit 0, matching importlib.metadata 0.16.0. Portability: pure Python string output; no subprocess, path, fd, signal or encoding change. make verify queued (host verify cap of 3).","timestamp":1795052470622174907},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on 4dced0093d6: exit 0 (21419 + 226 passed). Pushed as Gerrit change https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/3441.","timestamp":1795059860186102558},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged: change 3441 at 85ff756cf17e4b5cc624bb54f543d544e8a4872f (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1). On merged main: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py -k version` 3 passed; `python scripts/probe_rebar.py` 144 passed, 0 failed; mechanism gate exit 0; wheel built from merged main (`uv build --wheel`) into a fresh venv: `rebar --version` -> `rebar 0.16.0 (6f5f854be4c)`, exit 0, importlib.metadata 0.16.0. The commit in that local wheel is the checkout's previously generated `_build_info.py` (the build preserves an existing one); release builds set REBAR_BUILD_COMMIT, and wheel_test compares against `_build_info.COMMIT`, so this does not affect releases. Windows sweep not dispatched: the change adds stdout text only, no subprocess, fd, path, encoding or permission code.","timestamp":1795061918564850045}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794616397303729599,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cbf6fee0-159c-4276-9a67-1b553c1ad152","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6162-9672-915c-4909"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`rebar --version` exits 1 with `Error: unknown subcommand '--version'` and the overview, and no rebar command prints the installed version. Release checks (and users filing bugs) need the version and build commit. Observed 2026-11-13 on origin/main d6ba771 in an editable build and in a wheel; v0.15.1 lacks it too, so this is not a regression.\n\nOperator decision (2026-11-18, recorded in a ticket comment): option (1), a top-level `--version`, explicitly approved as an exception to the bug-fix no-new-flags rule.\n\n## Approach\nServe `--version` in `rebar._cli._help_route.pre_scan` (src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:162), the function that already serves `--help` and the unknown-subcommand error before any configuration, snapshot or store mount (`rebar._cli._main_dispatch` calls it first, src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:351). When the first residual token after the `-c` prefix is `--version`, write `rebar <version> (<commit>)` plus a newline to stdout and return 0.\n- `<version>` is `importlib.metadata.version(\"nava-rebar\")`; `unknown` on `PackageNotFoundError`.\n- `<commit>` is `rebar._build_info.COMMIT`, read with the same dynamic import `_baked_commit_sha` uses (src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py:129, which returns None when `_build_info` is absent); `unknown` when absent or empty. The import is dynamic because `_build_info.py` is generated at build time and git-ignored.\nServing it in pre_scan fits because it is the one place top-level flags are answered without touching the store, so `rebar --version` works outside any tracker. Only the exact token `--version` is accepted (no `-V`), keeping the new surface to the one approved flag. The overview help text is unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py: `--version` branch in `pre_scan` and a small `_version_line()` helper.\n- tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py: new tests next to the unknown-subcommand tests.\n- scripts/probe_rebar.py: assertions in the existing `--help` section (scripts/probe_rebar.py:564).\n- .github/workflows/release.yml: `wheel_test` \"Probe the installed wheel\" step checks `rebar --version` output against the installed metadata and baked COMMIT.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: `main([\"--version\"])` returns 0, stdout equals `rebar <metadata version> (<COMMIT>)\\n`, stderr empty.\n- With a `-c SECTION.KEY=VALUE` prefix, `--version` is still served.\n- Edge: `_build_info` missing (monkeypatched import failure) prints `(unknown)`; metadata missing prints `rebar unknown (...)`.\n- Unknown subcommands still error (existing `frobnicate` test unchanged).\n- Portability: pure Python, no subprocesses, paths, fds or signals; stdout text only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `rebar --version` exits 0 and prints `rebar <version> (<commit>)`. Checked: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py -k version` passes on merged main.\n- [x] A wheel install prints the installed version. Checked: build a wheel from merged main with `python -m build --wheel`, install it into a fresh venv, run `rebar --version`, and confirm exit 0 and that the version matches `importlib.metadata.version(\"nava-rebar\")` in that venv.\n- [x] `scripts/probe_rebar.py` asserts `rebar --version` exits 0 and prints a line starting `rebar `. Checked: `python scripts/probe_rebar.py` reports FAIL 0 on merged main.\n- [x] release.yml `wheel_test` probes `rebar --version`. Checked: reading the merged step, and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [x] The operator's choice is recorded on this ticket. Checked: the 2026-11-18 decision comment.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py","reason":"serve --version in pre_scan"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py","reason":"--version tests"},{"path":"scripts/probe_rebar.py","reason":"probe rebar --version"},{"path":".github/workflows/release.yml","reason":"wheel_test probes rebar --version"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6162-9672-915c-4909"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ea04f988-b553-489f-83bf-ecaa019e241b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d056-2825-e475-432b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar --version is rejected as an unknown subcommand","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["bd0e4053-6c6c-4e8b-8973-e6b457ac6bae","0e5e66fe-4bca-4a26-8d67-f36250172e50","451ee1a2-1388-4419-acab-5ef7bfb16c00","3e0aa95f-bc6f-460e-a5cb-69a6b2ff37df","ef16ccf8-077c-4551-80ad-2165cac82461","15365dbd-b345-4b66-8dd2-a06b232d5a4e","a31c22b8-cca0-4fef-a093-a16eb17c7ada","5801c032-d324-4fa3-b890-f28eb9c2cf4d","79101002-db79-4c9e-8e44-441c1a8e686d","cbf6fee0-159c-4276-9a67-1b553c1ad152","a1018db9-5de2-4937-81cc-3767fb6ed471","92085caf-224e-4d88-8046-8d9838d42242","c0182566-0c3e-4fe7-a6a3-38e03c5c2e2b","ea04f988-b553-489f-83bf-ecaa019e241b","72f3c015-9c49-4db6-ab3a-c453ca98d3b1"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795062475164686297,"uuid":"44e5c9b0-e138-4d62-a8ff-c2e5b878063c"}
